          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Name \"Linux\"</strong><br>\nThe name \"Linux\" comes from the Linux kernel, which Torvalds originally named \"Freax.\" It was meant to be a combination of \"free,\" \"freak,\" and \"Unix.\" However, the kernel was eventually renamed \"Linux\" by others, combining Linus's name with Unix.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Linux Kernel Version Control</strong><br>\nTorvalds also created Git, a version control system that is widely used in software development today. Git helps developers manage changes to source code over time, making it easier to collaborate on projects.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on Computing</strong><br>\nLinux has had a significant impact on the computing world. It runs on servers, desktops, mobile devices, and even embedded systems. Linux-based operating systems power much of the internet's infrastructure and are known for their stability and security.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
