            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Philosophy</strong><br>\nTorvalds has been known for his outspoken nature, especially regarding his personal philosophy on software development. He believes in practicality over idealism when it comes to creating software, which has guided the development of Linux.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Recognition and Awards</strong><br>\nFor his work on Linux, Torvalds has received numerous accolades, including the Millennium Technology Prize. This award is one of the most prestigious in the field of technology and innovation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Current Work</strong><br>\nToday, Linus Torvalds continues to oversee the development of the Linux kernel, coordinating the work of programmers from around the globe. His work remains central to the ongoing evolution of open-source software.</p>\n"
              },
